cing, with or without Dwarf wall not exceeding 0.60 mts.\nheight.\n15.\nFire license Compliance Certificate from DF&RS is required.\n16.\nOSR land As the OSR space is vested with competent authority/ Local Body, no structure shall be constructed / erected on OSR land.\n17.\nStructures permitted in Access steps to Ground floor and ramps, (without affecting ventilation of Basement Floor) closed Well, the set back area Water and Sewage Treatment Plant, Generator, Box type transformers are permitted in the set back area subject to availability of minimum set back of 6.7 mts.\nand satisfying the parking requirements.\n18.\nStructures permitted in AC Plant and Two toilets in every block are permitted in the Terrace Floor.\nArchitectural feature the Terrace Floor in the periphery on the top most floor (Terrace Floor) up to 3.00 mts.\nheight is permissible subject to the condition that the portion constructed over allowable 1.5 mts.\nheight parapet wall shall be non continuous with solid portion not exceeding 50% of the surface area.\n19.\nInstallation of Solar 1/3 rd area of the total terrace area to be reserved Energy System for erecting Solar Photo Voltaic Panels.\nThe approximate space required for erecting Solar Voltaic Panel is 10 sq.mt for generating 1 KW of electricity.\nHARMANDER SINGH, Principal Secretary to Government.\nPRINTED AND PUBLISHED BY THE DIRECTOR OF STATIONERY AND PRINTING, CHENNAI ON BEHALF OF THE GOVERNMENT OF TAMIL NADU. Provided: 2.0 m. Required: >= 12.0 m.", "[L124 Inference] IfcBeam 'YC-ST-SF-BIP' is NON-COMPLIANT. Rule: 13).\nThese holes specify the requirements of the information needed to fill them correctly.\nThe information providers then exchange the information deliverables with the information receiver thereby filling in the holes.\nInformation receiver Information provider creates the information provides the values to requirements satisfy them Some values may be pre-determined in the requirements (example performance ratings) Detailed i